<?xml version="1.0"?>
<configuration>
<startup><supportedRuntime version="v4.0" sku=".NETFramework,Version=v4.5.2"/></startup>

  <!--
    SECURITY - do NOT add WCF message logging or ServiceModel activity tracing to this file.

    This config previously enabled full WCF diagnostic message logging that wrote every internal SOAP
    message between SecureExamBrowser.exe and SebWindowsServiceWCF.exe - including auth tokens - to a
    plaintext trace file (RuntimeService trace) on every candidate machine. A cracked build was
    reverse-engineered directly from that trace. It has been removed.

    The WCF endpoint and binding are configured in code (ServiceUtils/SEBWindowsServiceController.cs),
    not here, so nothing functional depends on a system.serviceModel section in this file.

    Debug the IPC only in a LOCAL debug build, never committed. The release pipeline should fail if WCF
    diagnostic tracing reappears in any shipped .config.
  -->

</configuration>
